and today's January 6th and in  Washington today President Biden will  Mark The Assault on the capitol  occurring just exactly two years ago  he's going to honor some of the police  officers who fought with rioters that  day federal prosecutors of course have  charged more than 950 people and a  congressional panel investigating the  attack has heard from more than a  thousand Witnesses all detailing what  happened that day and as Scott McFarland  reports criminal trials continue but  some staffers are also still coping with  trauma yeah  go go as an angry mob climbed walls at  the Capitol  smashed Windows pushed back police  and threatened to hang the sitting vice  president Congressional staffer Sharon  Nichols was alone barricaded inside an  office worried about losing her life it  was frightening it was terrifying being  alone was the hardest part  very few rioters were arrested that day  the police were vastly outnumbered and  at times overpowered by the mob  but the FBI seized records from more  than 5 000 cell phones and amassed  thousands of hours of video of what may  be the most documented crime in U.S  history charging at least 950 people so  far nearly half of whom have either  pleaded guilty or been convicted at  trial including Oath Keepers founder  Stuart Rhodes convicted of seditious  conspiracy those in favor say aye  aye after an 18-month probe the U.S  House January 6th committee referred  former president Donald Trump to the  justice department for prosecution  alleging he incited an Insurrection  these people are not going to take it  any longer Trump has denied any  wrongdoing but already a declared 2024  presidential candidate a former Federal  prosecutor says if there are any  criminal charges they may come soon you  think if they were going to move on this  they'd want to move well before the next  Presidential election well before not  only that but if there is going to be  charge they want a trial to happen  before the next election as for Nichols  she still works here and started a  support group for other survivors it  helped us to connect with one another to  talk about it to share our experiences  with each other and compare  Capitol Police have suffered a series of  resignations and retirements after the  attack on their officers but they have a  new Chief who says they've made more  than 100 significant improvements in the  time since but he acknowledges there is  more hiring and more work still to be  done Adriana  Scott thank you so much in front of a  beautiful Capital this morning beautiful  but a little chaotic this morning
 

